course: dictionary
lesson: 1760
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word cleansing comes from the verb cleanse, which means to make something very clean. When a nurse washes a cut with clean water, she is cleansing it, so germs cannot get in. Cleansing can be a verb, a noun or an adjective, depending on how it is used.
explain: A word with more than one meaning needs its context to show which meaning you need. In «cleansing wipes» it describes what the wipes are for, so it is an adjective. In «a cleansing cry» it means a cry that gets bad feelings out of you. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: Be careful with one phrase. «"Ethnic cleansing" means driving out or killing a whole ethnic group (a people who share family roots, language or customs) from an area.» This is a horrible crime. The soft word cleansing hides how cruel it really is. This is called a euphemism, and when you meet one, ask what the words really mean.
fact: Cleanse is the verb; cleansing is its -ing form and can also be a noun or an adjective.
fact: «Cleansing» can mean making something very clean, like «cleansing a cut» with clean water to stop germs.
fact: Cleansing products, such as face cleanser and cleansing wipes, are used for washing skin.
fact: A «cleansing cry» means a cry that gets bad feelings out of your system.
fact: «Ethnic cleansing» is a euphemism: a soft-sounding phrase for a horrible crime against a whole group of people, which history lessons teach us to recognise.
exercise: «The nurse cleaned the cut with clean water, cleansing it to stop germs.» What does cleansing mean here? | Breaking something open | Running very fast | Hiding a cut under a bandage | *Making something very clean
exercise: Mum buys a new face cleanser. What is a face cleanser used for? | Keeping your feet warm | Cooking dinner | *Washing your face | Painting a wall
exercise: Ella says, «A cleansing cry helped me feel better.» What does cleansing mean in this sentence? | Singing loudly | Washing her hair | Making the room tidy | *Getting rid of bad feelings
test: Dad bought cleansing wipes for the baby. What kind of word is cleansing here? | Verb | *Adjective | Noun | Adverb
test: «Ethnic cleansing» is called a euphemism. What is a euphemism? | A word that means the opposite of another word | *A soft-sounding word or phrase that hides something harsh | A very long word | A word from another country
exam: Why should we look beyond a soft word like «cleansing» when it is used for something cruel? | *To find out what it really means | Because soft words are always wrong | Because it helps us learn how to wash | To make the sentence sound more exciting
